kern-qwen38

CUDA operators and FlashInfer adapters are adapted from the Apache-2.0 projects
kern (b118a55c55f236a37046f54f066ecb8e6c12caff), kern-qwen3
(ca9199117bec3c85d13b3ed5869243af23e2f80a), and pegainfer
(dc78afb0873f53606ad494d5a899f0fdbf0687df).
See upstreams.json for per-file origins and original hashes.

FlashInfer is an unmodified git submodule pinned to
023a8474e1f7469572c0d4284535fc6ffa699574 (main HEAD at import time).
Its headers are instantiated through local CUDA adapters.
See third_party/flashinfer/LICENSE and its upstream copyright notices.

Local adaptations add BF16 persistent GDN state with FP32 register updates,
FP8 cache writes with explicit scales, GQA=6 attention instantiations,
and a block-scaled FP8 weight GEMV candidate derived from pegainfer's
streaming warp-per-row approach.

source/gdn_prefill.py adapts pegainfer's Apache-2.0 chunked GDN source,
which attributes the original algorithms to Flash Linear Attention (FLA),
https://github.com/fla-org/flash-linear-attention. The original file-level
attribution is preserved. Local changes handle BA strides and numerical rules.

DSpine bridge and greedy refinement kernels are adapted from Tencent/DSpine
(https://github.com/Tencent/DSpine), licensed under Apache-2.0.

ReplaySSM verification is adapted from Tencent/DSpine; compact state materialization
is adapted from SGLang v0.5.22 (https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang), Apache-2.0.
SGLang attributes its ReplaySSM implementation to Johnny-Liou/ReplaySSM
(commit 3c85112, vLLM reference) and the Dao AI Lab ReplaySSM algorithm.
